{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "transport_flux_divergence_layered",
  "description": "B-grid lowering rule of the conservative flux-form tracer divergence rewrite target D(c*u, x) + D(c*v, y) for a per-category per-layer tracer c on the T cells advected by the B-grid corner velocities uvel/vvel on the U points: the layered companion of transport_flux_divergence, matching the same compound two-term sum with params c/u/v as wildcards and where-shape constraints (c: [i,j,ncat,layer], u: [i,j], v: [i,j], esm-spec 9.6.1) and emitting the [i,j,ncat,layer] makearray of the conservative cell divergence div = (F_e(i,j) - F_e(i-1,j) + F_n(i,j) - F_n(i,j-1)) / tarea(i,j) (the Fortran mass update mm = mm - (mflxe(i,j) - mflxe(i-1,j) + mflxn(i,j) - mflxn(i,j-1))*tarear, ice_transport_remap.F90:3586-3590). The layer axis is a passive extra axis: the same edge fluxes/areas apply per layer, so the rule applies the transport_flux_divergence_cell stencil (the east/north edge fluxes are the centered corner-average reconstructions F_e = HTE*((uS + uN)/2)*((cL + cR)/2) and F_n = HTN*((vW + vE)/2)*((cS + cN)/2) of the scalar atoms transport_flux_e/n, exactly the Fortran's edge-area reconstruction edgearea_e/n, ice_transport_remap.F90:658-666, the linear branch) at every layer l with the same neighbor bindings, so the 12 per-layer enthalpy products (vqicen_1..8, vsqsnon_1..3) of the per-layer formulation collapse to the two 4-D unknowns vqicen[i,j,ncat,layer] and vsqsnon[i,j,ncat,layer]. The makearray tiles the same nine i/j position classes as transport_flux_divergence (interior [2..N_I-1]x[2..N_J-1], the four strips i = 1, i = N_I, j = 1, j = N_J, and the four corners) times the full layer range [1..N_LAYER], with halo-copy closures: every neighbor index that leaves the domain (c, u/v, HTE/HTN at i-1, i+1, j-1, j+1) is bound to the nearest interior value, reproducing the Fortran's ice_HaloUpdate of the transported fields and edge lengths. NOTE: the traced Fortran run integrates the incremental-remap transport (departure-region integrals over the limited linear reconstruction, transport_integrals, ice_transport_remap.F90:3188-3472), whose per-cell flux differs from this centered face average by O(C) slope corrections; the scheme difference is documented with the stage-2 transport pins.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "esd:rule",
   "family:cice_bgrid",
   "grid:cice_bgrid",
   "op:D",
   "axes:i,j,ncat,layer",
   "order:1",
   "form:flux",
   "bc:halo-copy",
   "stagger:b",
   "spec:9.6.8"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), the horizontal transport edge reconstruction."
   }
  ]
 },
 "expression_template_imports": [
  {
   "ref": "../stencils/transport_flux_divergence_cell.esm"
  }
 ],
